          "story": {
            "text": "Saturday's 2-5 loss to #4 Sting Attack was a gut punch — no other way to say it. Against one of the division's best, McNeal gave up three in the second half when it mattered most. That stings.\n\nBut here's what doesn't change: 6 wins, 19 points, and one game left. This team has beaten teams ranked ahead of them all season. They've come back from multi-match losing skids before. The record shows a squad that competes — 23 goals scored, a win over #6 LC United, back-to-back wins in February when the season needed it most.\n\nThe final opponent is #17 Sting G13 Hubbard. On paper, this is a winnable game. But the only way it matters is if this team shows up with something to prove. A loss on Saturday can't define the season — the response to it can.\n\nSit at #11 of 18 with 19 points, and 3 more on the table Tuesday night. One game. One chance to finish with your head up.\n\nThe season isn't over. Write a better ending.",
